# @BUNNY_APP_NAME@

A [bunny-ui](https://github.com/thebunnylab/bunny_ui) app.

## Run it

```bash
bunny run              # on this computer
bunny run -d ios       # in the iOS Simulator
bunny run -d android   # on an Android emulator or phone
bunny run -d web       # in the browser
```

`bunny run` reloads hot on this computer, in the iOS Simulator and on Android:
save a file and the running app takes the new code, its state kept. `bunny doctor` says what
each platform still needs on this machine, and `bunny devices` lists where the
app can run. On the desktop, `cargo run` works too.

## Where things are

- `src/lib.rs` — the app. `bunny_ui::app!` at its end starts it on every
  platform.
- `src/main.rs` — the desktop and iOS entry; it only calls `run()`.
- `Cargo.toml` — `[package.metadata.bunny]` holds the name people read and
  the id every platform files the app under.
- `android/`, `ios/`, `macos/`, `web/` — each platform's own files. They are
  yours to edit; `bunny` fills the `@BUNNY_…@` markers in them on every
  build, and keeps `.bunny-template` to know which template they came from.
